WEBVTT

00:04.500 --> 00:05.900
Counting on you, man.

00:06.730 --> 00:08.490
Hey, Ayanokoji.

00:08.490 --> 00:10.850
You're taking this quiz challenge, too?

00:11.210 --> 00:14.920
Yeah. Are things going 
well for your group?

00:14.920 --> 00:17.140
We're racking up the game points!

00:17.140 --> 00:17.950
But...

00:18.350 --> 00:22.200
It's Kanji, you know? 
He's acting pretty down.

00:22.840 --> 00:25.460
He'd been a little weird 
before the test, too,

00:25.760 --> 00:28.350
but he keeps trying to 
pretend like he's fine.

00:29.020 --> 00:31.660
I'm worried, but we're in a challenge now.

00:32.030 --> 00:36.160
Work together and you 
should place near the top.

00:36.160 --> 00:37.210
Right.

00:37.340 --> 00:39.950
But you're by yourself, right?

00:39.950 --> 00:41.100
You gonna be okay?

00:41.330 --> 00:45.230
It will depend on if the category 
is one of my strong fields.

00:45.230 --> 00:47.580
Well, see ya later.

00:47.580 --> 00:49.890
Like you said, we're in a challenge now.

00:49.890 --> 00:51.610
We're gonna give it our all!

00:51.950 --> 00:53.620
Let us begin.

00:53.620 --> 00:54.610
Topic: Anime Trivia

00:55.470 --> 00:56.610
Anime?

00:56.610 --> 00:59.620
<b>Question 1
 In the TV anime <i>Mobile Servant Bomdam</i>,
which of the following is the title of Episode 13?</b>

00:57.660 --> 00:58.760
What in the world?

00:58.840 --> 00:59.620
<b>1. Farewell, Bomdam</b>

00:58.950 --> 00:59.620
<b>2. Burn, Bomdam</b>

00:59.080 --> 00:59.620
<b>3. Shout, Bomdam</b>

00:59.210 --> 00:59.620
<b>4. The Tears of Bomdam</b>

00:59.620 --> 01:01.950
Are you kidding?! Easiest challenge ever!

01:02.260 --> 01:03.700
All right, but...

01:04.370 --> 01:07.250
What in the world is Bomdam?

01:17.520 --> 01:23.320
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

02:27.380 --> 02:33.930
Classroom of the Elite 4th Season 2nd Year 1st Term

02:38.980 --> 02:40.890
All right! First place is ours!

02:40.890 --> 02:42.260
Great work, man!

02:42.650 --> 02:44.150
Kanji!

02:43.850 --> 02:46.270
<b>#10 Love Uncommunicated</b>

02:44.150 --> 02:46.290
R-Right!

02:47.020 --> 02:49.320
That quiz was very challenging.

02:49.320 --> 02:50.310
Yeah.

02:52.230 --> 02:56.170
Are you worried about Sudo-senpai's group?

02:56.170 --> 02:58.030
What do you think of them?

02:58.260 --> 03:01.780
The one sitting on the 
ground seems disheartened.

03:02.000 --> 03:03.970
Is he feeling ill, perhaps?

03:04.360 --> 03:06.540
It's not a physical issue.

03:06.540 --> 03:10.530
You're worried about a psychological 
issue on their part, then?

03:10.530 --> 03:14.920
I won't deny it, but I don't 
have time to worry about others.

03:16.260 --> 03:19.460
The fourth designated area 
will be announced soon.

03:19.460 --> 03:20.840
Shall we get going?

03:20.840 --> 03:22.540
First, Nanase...

03:22.920 --> 03:25.300
Could I look at your tablet?

03:25.620 --> 03:26.810
Fair enough.

03:27.150 --> 03:30.270
We don't know for sure that 
we're on the same table yet.

03:30.270 --> 03:33.770
<i>I thought she might refuse, but...</i>

03:34.820 --> 03:38.240
It seems we really are 
on the same table, then.

03:38.240 --> 03:39.380
Agreed.

03:39.380 --> 03:41.380
Shall we take the shortest route?

03:41.380 --> 03:44.160
No, let's not force ourselves.

03:44.510 --> 03:48.040
Challenges have spawned at G8 and G9, too.

03:48.290 --> 03:52.040
Let's visit those two and call it a day.

03:52.040 --> 03:54.820
Where should we camp tonight, then?

03:54.820 --> 03:56.070
Good question.

03:56.730 --> 04:00.800
Once we've done the challenges, 
let's walk to H9 and camp there.

04:01.570 --> 04:03.230
Hey, Ayanokoji.

04:03.230 --> 04:05.700
Did you say you were gonna camp in H9?

04:06.030 --> 04:07.800
What if I did?

04:07.800 --> 04:10.560
That's our next designated area.

04:10.900 --> 04:13.510
You wanna meet up later?

04:13.510 --> 04:15.810
It's always more fun with friends around.

04:15.810 --> 04:18.110
I'd love to pick your brain, too.

04:18.110 --> 04:19.420
Sure thing.

04:19.420 --> 04:21.650
Do you have any issue with that, Nanase?

04:21.650 --> 04:22.700
Not at all.

04:23.160 --> 04:26.180
I'd see it as a fine 
opportunity to talk, in fact.

04:30.390 --> 04:32.910
Nanase-chan, you're in Class D?

04:33.170 --> 04:35.700
You don't look like the type to me.

04:35.700 --> 04:39.170
Not at all. I'm actually 
quite a mess of a person.

04:39.170 --> 04:41.660
It's appropriate that 
I'd start in Class D.

04:41.660 --> 04:44.300
Aw, you don't look like a mess to me.

04:44.540 --> 04:47.930
We're the real messes, right?

04:49.060 --> 04:51.180
Kanji, Ken, what's with you guys?

04:52.030 --> 04:53.680
We're fine.

04:53.930 --> 04:55.650
But Ryotaro...

04:55.650 --> 04:58.110
You really shouldn't trust Nanase.

04:58.110 --> 05:00.070
Huh? How come?

05:00.380 --> 05:02.240
It's just the truth.

05:02.240 --> 05:03.860
I don't follow.

05:03.860 --> 05:05.580
It's all right, Hondo-senpai.

05:05.960 --> 05:10.070
I did something hurtful 
to Sudo-senpai before.

05:10.380 --> 05:11.880
Something hurtful?

05:11.880 --> 05:14.010
I don't wanna talk about it.

05:14.540 --> 05:16.620
Well, okay.

05:16.620 --> 05:19.170
But Kanji, you've been 
down for a while, huh?

05:20.200 --> 05:23.270
No way, man. I'm just... fine.

05:23.270 --> 05:25.290
You're clearly not fine!

05:25.290 --> 05:28.250
You've been acting weird 
since before the test.

05:28.250 --> 05:30.040
Ganging up on me now, huh?

05:30.440 --> 05:33.050
I-I'm fine, like I said...

05:33.720 --> 05:37.130
You seem rather listless to me, as well.

05:37.460 --> 05:38.440
See?

05:38.440 --> 05:40.770
Has something been bothering you?

05:42.830 --> 05:45.690
Well... it's just...

05:45.930 --> 05:48.970
C'mon. Just spill it already, man.

05:48.970 --> 05:51.160
It's probably nothing serious, right?

05:53.550 --> 05:55.300
It's really nothing.

05:55.790 --> 05:58.100
Why not give him time 
to collect his thoughts?

05:58.100 --> 05:58.940
Huh?

06:02.100 --> 06:04.810
No need for that, Nanase-chan.

06:05.470 --> 06:08.120
Nah. Let's give him time, Ryotaro.

06:08.920 --> 06:10.430
S-Sure.

06:10.430 --> 06:11.970
Fine. Okay.

06:14.260 --> 06:16.380
The truth is, um...

06:18.070 --> 06:19.060
There's...

06:19.700 --> 06:23.570
There's a girl I've kind of... 
liked... for a while.

06:24.230 --> 06:26.070
The girl I like...

06:26.600 --> 06:28.470
The girl I've fallen for...

06:30.210 --> 06:32.780
It's, um...

06:33.590 --> 06:36.140
Shinohara Satsuki.

06:37.070 --> 06:38.940
I hated her at first.

06:39.720 --> 06:42.580
But... I can't really explain it...

06:42.580 --> 06:44.800
At some point, I started liking her.

06:44.800 --> 06:49.610
But I didn't want to admit it, so I 
pretended I didn't like her at all.

06:50.120 --> 06:53.430
So why not just fess up to her already?

06:53.430 --> 06:55.930
I can't do that now, can I?!

06:56.550 --> 06:58.110
Something happened, didn't it?

06:58.970 --> 07:02.020
Komiya's in the group she ended up in.

07:03.230 --> 07:04.860
I think he...

07:06.310 --> 07:08.730
He probably likes her, too.

07:10.190 --> 07:15.100
And Shinohara... I think maybe 
she has eyes for him, too.

07:17.070 --> 07:20.860
So... I wanted to get her 
in my group for this test.

07:21.550 --> 07:24.050
But I just couldn't be honest.

07:24.380 --> 07:26.960
It ended in a fight like usual.

07:27.700 --> 07:29.340
I'm so pathetic.

07:30.440 --> 07:33.840
I think I got the wrong 
idea at some point...

07:34.210 --> 07:39.350
Even though we've fought, 
I thought maybe she liked me, too...

07:40.430 --> 07:42.100
I'm lame as all hell.

07:42.970 --> 07:45.870
I still dunno what to do.

07:46.750 --> 07:48.110
Ike-senpai...

07:48.430 --> 07:52.360
You have trouble being honest 
with Shinohara-senpai, don't you?

07:52.980 --> 07:56.620
I don't think there's 
anything wrong with that.

07:56.620 --> 07:59.870
But now Shinohara's in 
a group with Komiya!

07:59.870 --> 08:01.930
That means I'm friend-zoned 
for good, right?!

08:02.260 --> 08:06.000
I don't know. I really don't, but...

08:06.690 --> 08:10.760
Shinohara-senpai might be waiting 
for you to make a gesture.

08:11.420 --> 08:12.630
Make a gesture?

08:12.860 --> 08:16.230
It's clear that you're the kind of 
person who's friendly with everyone

08:16.230 --> 08:19.640
and says what's on his mind.

08:20.200 --> 08:24.520
Shinohara-senpai probably 
likes that about you.

08:25.130 --> 08:32.150
But she also wants to be a 
little more special to you.

08:33.310 --> 08:38.540
She wanted you to be a little more 
open about the fact that you like her.

08:40.500 --> 08:42.560
It's fine to protect your heart,

08:42.560 --> 08:45.290
but you won't get anywhere 
until you tell her how you feel.

08:45.610 --> 08:49.040
I understand you wanting 
to go after her now, too,

08:49.350 --> 08:52.170
but your first priority should 
be surviving this trial.

08:53.100 --> 08:54.870
If you find yourself unable 
to see her again...

08:56.220 --> 08:58.790
If you end up in a situation where 
you can't see the person you love...

09:00.420 --> 09:05.900
you'll never have another chance 
to tell them how you feel.

09:07.350 --> 09:11.260
This is no time to wallow in 
your feelings, Ike-senpai.

09:11.790 --> 09:12.840
You're right.

09:13.460 --> 09:17.970
None of it means anything unless 
I survive this test, right?

09:17.970 --> 09:20.660
I can't get anywhere if 
I'm outside the school.

09:20.660 --> 09:22.580
Yeah! That's the way, Kanji!

09:32.280 --> 09:34.630
Um, Ayanokoji-senpai...

09:34.880 --> 09:36.500
Are you awake?

09:36.860 --> 09:38.540
Give me a minute.

09:38.540 --> 09:39.890
I'll come out.

09:40.820 --> 09:45.860
Do you think I went too far in what 
I said to Ike-senpai yesterday?

09:46.520 --> 09:48.970
Your words reinvigorated him.

09:49.550 --> 09:51.400
He's probably grateful.

09:51.630 --> 09:53.270
Do you think so?

09:53.880 --> 09:57.950
I feel like he may be 
in a precarious place.

09:58.630 --> 10:03.450
What I said earlier might lead 
him to push himself too far...

10:03.910 --> 10:07.480
So I'm worried about leaving him.

10:07.870 --> 10:10.250
I understand how you feel.

10:10.920 --> 10:14.050
But we can't stay with him, huh?

10:14.590 --> 10:19.130
Well, if we decide on a place to 
meet up, we can meet up again.

10:19.580 --> 10:22.210
The designated areas could 
throw a wrench into that,

10:22.210 --> 10:24.180
but let's arrange it before we part ways.

10:24.180 --> 10:26.890
All right. Thank you.

10:39.890 --> 10:43.910
So this challenge is "beach flags."

10:44.490 --> 10:45.910
I'd like to register.

10:45.910 --> 10:46.520
Right.

10:52.660 --> 10:54.580
Is registration still open?

10:54.580 --> 10:58.400
I'm afraid we just filled up.

10:58.400 --> 10:59.660
I see.

10:59.970 --> 11:02.930
There's room for one more in 
the women's event, though.

11:03.290 --> 11:07.150
If you can't participate, I'll pass.

11:07.460 --> 11:10.620
No, I wanted a break anyway.

11:10.620 --> 11:12.450
You should take part.

11:12.450 --> 11:13.810
But...

11:14.200 --> 11:17.880
The fact that you've yielded 
the arrival order awards to me

11:17.880 --> 11:20.100
is giving me a healthy game-point cushion.

11:20.750 --> 11:22.320
Thank you.

11:22.660 --> 11:24.950
I'll take you up on that offer.

11:24.950 --> 11:27.830
<i>Everyone else here is a third-year.</i>

11:28.200 --> 11:31.630
<i>If only one from each 
group can participate,</i>

11:31.630 --> 11:33.400
<i>it shouldn't be so unbalanced.</i>

11:34.200 --> 11:37.510
<i>I wonder if they've gathered 
here for some purpose.</i>

11:39.720 --> 11:42.470
Um... how should I put this...

11:42.470 --> 11:45.280
You picked a very cute swimsuit.

11:45.280 --> 11:46.440
Really?

11:46.440 --> 11:51.050
I was pretty sure this is what 
beach flag players wear on TV...

11:51.050 --> 11:53.730
Did I get it wrong?

11:53.730 --> 11:54.850
No.

11:55.210 --> 11:58.730
<i>Her Physical Ability on the OAA is B+.</i>

11:59.020 --> 12:01.520
<i>But from what I've seen from her so far,</i>

12:01.520 --> 12:04.870
<i>I wouldn't be surprised 
if she earned an A.</i>

12:05.810 --> 12:08.740
U-Um, Ayanokoji-senpai...

12:08.740 --> 12:13.450
Having you stare at me like that 
makes me feel a little self-conscious...

12:13.450 --> 12:15.320
Oh, right.

12:15.320 --> 12:16.250
Sorry.

12:17.370 --> 12:19.250
Well, I'll be on my way.

12:24.760 --> 12:26.290
Here I go!

12:30.340 --> 12:34.300
It looks like you missed 
your shot at the challenge.

12:34.300 --> 12:36.370
I suppose you did, too.

12:36.900 --> 12:41.030
Or are you just here because 
it's your designated area?

12:41.030 --> 12:43.030
I couldn't say.

12:43.330 --> 12:45.080
Would you like to swim with me?

12:45.080 --> 12:47.420
You seem to be taking 
a leisurely approach.

12:47.730 --> 12:51.230
I assumed you'd be scrambling 
to win game points.

12:51.910 --> 12:54.040
It's important to take breaks, as well.

12:54.320 --> 12:57.550
Besides, things don't kick 
into gear until tomorrow.

12:57.870 --> 12:59.930
That's when the mid-game begins.

12:59.930 --> 13:04.340
The top and bottom ten 
groups will be announced.

13:04.340 --> 13:08.680
If any non-third-year groups have 
wedged themselves into the top three,

13:08.680 --> 13:10.720
that's when I'll move into action.

13:10.720 --> 13:14.350
We can't have any first- or second-years 
standing on the victory podium.

13:14.350 --> 13:16.110
That includes you, of course.

13:16.110 --> 13:18.990
I appreciate the warning.

13:19.340 --> 13:22.290
But I'm by myself,

13:22.290 --> 13:25.040
so I'm more likely to end up 
at the bottom, if anything.

13:25.040 --> 13:29.620
You'd better form a group soon, then.

13:29.850 --> 13:32.870
If you end up self-destructing 
and getting yourself expelled,

13:33.220 --> 13:36.350
I think Horikita-senpai 
will be very disappointed.

13:37.010 --> 13:39.500
Nagumo, could you come here a minute?

13:42.130 --> 13:45.940
<i>There's a strategy Nagumo Miyabi 
is uniquely cut out for.</i>

13:46.750 --> 13:49.060
<i>If he carries it out...</i>

13:50.140 --> 13:53.980
<i>It could be a very 
difficult battle indeed.</i>

13:59.410 --> 14:01.020
You won easily.

14:01.020 --> 14:04.030
Thank you. It didn't feel easy, though.

14:04.030 --> 14:06.700
Nanase, how are your water supplies?

14:06.700 --> 14:10.780
I'm almost out, aside from 
this bottle I just won.

14:10.780 --> 14:13.100
I'm down to one bottle, too.

14:13.100 --> 14:15.850
The first real hurdle will 
be securing hydration.

14:15.850 --> 14:18.770
We'll have to find water somehow.

14:19.920 --> 14:24.190
<i>If I were by myself, I could continually 
return to the starting area to restock,</i>

14:24.190 --> 14:27.920
<i>hitting designated areas and 
challenges along the way.</i>

14:28.360 --> 14:31.230
<i>But I doubt Nanase can keep up with that.</i>

14:31.700 --> 14:33.310
Ayanokoji-senpai.

14:33.660 --> 14:36.680
Why did you decide to work alone?

14:37.060 --> 14:38.340
Are you worried about me?

14:38.650 --> 14:43.060
I just don't see any 
benefit to working alone.

14:43.470 --> 14:45.720
True, it comes with many disadvantages.

14:45.720 --> 14:47.940
But it's not without its benefits.

14:48.210 --> 14:51.450
Joining up with a group that's worried 
about falling behind in game points

14:51.820 --> 14:54.890
could provide unexpected 
synergistic effects.

14:54.890 --> 14:57.890
And that's why you're acting on your own?

14:57.890 --> 14:59.710
It's one possibility.

14:59.710 --> 15:04.790
Maybe you've simply overestimated me, 
and I failed to find a group to join.

15:05.740 --> 15:06.940
I suppose.

15:07.290 --> 15:11.470
You're not always the most eloquent 
person, Ayanokoji-senpai.

15:12.170 --> 15:14.140
Have you always been that way?

15:14.410 --> 15:19.730
Don't people with personalities like 
mine tend to stay consistently that way?

15:20.690 --> 15:27.230
But there are incidents that 
can change a person, I'm sure.

15:29.430 --> 15:33.560
What about you? Have you changed 
since you were in middle school?

15:33.940 --> 15:37.530
I'm not sure. 
I suppose I have, a little bit.

15:39.230 --> 15:40.830
In what way?

15:40.830 --> 15:44.500
I think I used to laugh more.

15:45.240 --> 15:51.540
I used to talk to people and 
have fun more often, too.

15:53.020 --> 15:55.370
Then there was an event...

15:56.490 --> 15:59.100
that made me feel like 
I really had changed.

16:05.980 --> 16:07.140
Can you keep going?

16:07.140 --> 16:08.830
Y-Yes.

16:09.430 --> 16:12.360
It's important to take breaks 
and not overtax yourself.

16:12.650 --> 16:13.990
But...

16:14.580 --> 16:17.620
If you push too hard now 
and can't keep up later,

16:17.620 --> 16:20.470
it'll probably be harder for you.

16:20.470 --> 16:23.370
Yes... That's true.

16:23.610 --> 16:25.810
I'll check out the challenge nearby.

16:29.300 --> 16:30.990
Can I register?

16:30.990 --> 16:33.700
Yes. You'll be the seventh.

16:34.130 --> 16:35.220
Can I register?!

16:35.650 --> 16:37.810
Your group will be the last.

16:40.220 --> 16:42.890
Hey, first time seeing you in this test,

16:43.210 --> 16:44.640
Ayanokoji.

16:44.990 --> 16:47.650
It takes courage to take this on solo.

16:47.650 --> 16:50.780
You racking up those game points?

16:50.780 --> 16:55.050
To be honest, I wouldn't be 
surprised if I'm in the bottom ten.

16:55.050 --> 16:56.770
Yeah, right.

16:56.770 --> 17:01.290
You wouldn't go it alone if you 
didn't think you could do it.

17:01.290 --> 17:05.670
I expect to see you in the top ten. Right?

17:05.980 --> 17:09.450
Anyway, I'm just glad this 
challenge isn't math.

17:09.820 --> 17:12.600
I don't stand a chance 
against a math genius.

17:12.600 --> 17:15.930
We will now begin the history challenge.

17:15.930 --> 17:18.760
No more talking, I guess.

17:16.890 --> 17:18.760
<b>Topic: History</b>

17:18.760 --> 17:20.760
<b>Question 1
 Which of the following is known as the shogun
with the most children in history?</b>

17:19.990 --> 17:20.760
<b>1.Tokugawa Iemitsu</b>

17:20.100 --> 17:20.760
<b>2. Tokugawa Tsunayoshi</b>

17:20.230 --> 17:20.760
<b>3. Tokugawa Yoshimune</b>

17:20.350 --> 17:20.760
<b>4. Tokugawa Ienari</b>

17:22.570 --> 17:25.020
Man, you got me again.

17:25.020 --> 17:28.020
I can't believe you're 
good at history, too.

17:28.020 --> 17:30.340
It was multiple choice. 
I got lucky at guessing.

17:30.340 --> 17:31.270
Lucky?

17:31.540 --> 17:34.150
Sorry, but I'm not buying that one.

17:34.150 --> 17:36.520
I'm afraid I'm in a hurry.

17:37.180 --> 17:39.990
Which challenge are you after next?

17:40.990 --> 17:43.910
I plan to hit the science challenge.

17:44.260 --> 17:46.390
That's a shame.

17:46.390 --> 17:48.870
Later, Ayanokoji.

17:53.210 --> 17:55.420
Nanase, how are you feeling?

17:55.420 --> 17:57.550
I feel ready to resume, thank you.

17:57.550 --> 17:59.570
Let's head out, then.

17:59.900 --> 18:03.930
Um, could I ask you a question?

18:04.210 --> 18:05.230
What is it?

18:05.230 --> 18:10.690
If I'm not mistaken, I think you 
could do much better if you wanted.

18:11.130 --> 18:13.880
In both the designated 
areas and the challenges.

18:14.430 --> 18:17.200
I fully intend to pace myself.

18:17.200 --> 18:21.620
But there are only so many game 
points you can score in a day.

18:21.940 --> 18:24.940
Won't you keep losing ground at this rate?

18:26.710 --> 18:30.960
All I'll say is that this is 
another part of my strategy.

18:30.960 --> 18:33.960
Your... strategy?

18:34.700 --> 18:36.100
Anyway, let's get going.

18:36.100 --> 18:37.590
R-Right.

18:41.490 --> 18:44.330
Sudo's group should be nearby.

18:44.330 --> 18:45.580
True.

18:45.580 --> 18:48.600
Hey, Ayanokoji!

18:49.420 --> 18:51.600
That was fast.

18:51.600 --> 18:54.110
We get to camp together again, huh?

18:54.510 --> 18:56.110
Amazing work.

18:56.110 --> 18:57.860
You caught all these fish?

18:59.400 --> 19:01.870
We caught 'em from the ocean.

19:01.870 --> 19:04.550
Hey, something smells delicious.

19:06.700 --> 19:08.640
What's wrong, Karuizawa-san?

19:08.640 --> 19:10.470
O-Oh, nothing.

19:10.470 --> 19:12.880
It's just, you know...

19:12.880 --> 19:15.550
It's pretty cool that 
they're frying those fish!

19:16.350 --> 19:19.620
Hey, mind if we camp out with you?

19:19.620 --> 19:22.110
Looks like Ike-kun's got a feast for us!

19:22.110 --> 19:24.140
Huh? Why should I share?!

19:24.140 --> 19:26.890
C'mon, it won't hurt you.

19:26.890 --> 19:28.400
It will if you eat <i>my</i> fish!

19:28.400 --> 19:29.730
Not happening!

19:29.730 --> 19:31.560
Hey, it's no big deal.

19:31.560 --> 19:34.500
She might know what Shinohara's up to.

19:35.770 --> 19:38.100
F-Fine, I guess.

19:38.100 --> 19:41.400
I'll fry up some extra, then!

19:41.400 --> 19:43.620
Really? Lucky us!

19:43.620 --> 19:45.530
I'm so glad we asked!

19:49.850 --> 19:51.430
Things seem to be going well.

19:51.430 --> 19:54.650
Yeah, no thanks to me.

19:55.880 --> 19:58.690
Has anything happened 
in the last few days?

19:59.030 --> 20:02.060
With the person you mentioned?

20:03.270 --> 20:05.730
Nothing in particular.

20:05.730 --> 20:09.370
They're writing down everyone they've 
interacted with on their tablet.

20:10.040 --> 20:11.640
Keep it up, please.

20:11.860 --> 20:13.130
Okay.

20:14.310 --> 20:16.390
While we're asking questions...

20:18.330 --> 20:20.280
That first-year...

20:20.280 --> 20:23.400
I hear she's been going around with you.

20:23.810 --> 20:24.890
Does that upset you?

20:27.870 --> 20:30.110
Of course it does.

20:30.420 --> 20:32.880
It's to do better on the test.

20:32.880 --> 20:35.020
I didn't have a choice. That's all.

20:35.560 --> 20:36.790
Really?

20:37.050 --> 20:39.530
That's the only emotion I have about it.

20:39.970 --> 20:41.690
I trust you, but...

20:42.150 --> 20:42.800
It's just...

20:43.490 --> 20:46.800
The thought of you being 
alone with a girl...

20:47.050 --> 20:48.430
I don't like it.

20:49.230 --> 20:49.930
Kei.

21:08.490 --> 21:10.250
Y-You kissed me?

21:11.750 --> 21:13.580
You can keep the faith, can't you?

21:35.780 --> 21:38.140
Is that an emergency alarm?

21:38.140 --> 21:40.730
It does seem likely.

21:41.340 --> 21:43.610
It doesn't seem like it's stopping.

21:43.980 --> 21:46.030
And if five minutes pass...

21:46.340 --> 21:52.490
Help will track down 
their location via GPS.

21:52.970 --> 21:57.610
Could we find them before 
the school comes?

21:57.610 --> 22:00.750
If we try, it would be 
better to have more people.

22:01.010 --> 22:02.850
Let's wake up the others.

22:04.260 --> 22:05.100
Right.
